# Live badge canvas box

iPhone Safari does not give an in-flow `height: 100%` child a box inside the aspect-ratio badge slot. The poster is absolute, so it still shows, and a collapsed canvas never paints or receives a drag. Desktop will not catch this.

Read `docs/adr/0001-live-badge-canvas-box.md` before changing `BadgeSlot`, the GLB canvas, the poster overlay, or `BadgeModelScene`.

## Required

- Slot content and the canvas fill the square with `absolute inset-0`. The canvas stays at full opacity when its WebGL context is created. The poster covers it until the model is ready.
- Studio HDR sits in its own Suspense and error boundary. It must not suspend the model.

## Do not

- Size the live canvas with in-flow `h-full` / `height: 100%` inside the aspect-ratio frame.
- Hide the canvas with `opacity-0` until visual ready.
- Put `Environment` and `BadgeModelContent` under one Suspense boundary.
- Treat a `powerPreference` or other iPhone-only renderer flag as the fix.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — percentage height in the flex square; canvas faded out before it can present
<div className="relative flex aspect-square">
  <Canvas className="h-full w-full" style={{ opacity: 0 }} />
</div>

// ✅ GOOD — absolute fill, canvas opaque, poster on top until ready
<div className="relative flex aspect-square">
  <div className="absolute inset-0">
    <Canvas style={{ position: "absolute", inset: 0, width: "100%", height: "100%" }} />
  </div>
</div>
```
